Projective Legendre matrices modulo3: (1, 2, 0, 1) (1, 0, 1, 1) (1, 1, 2, 0)
Group order: 12 ; commutator subgroup order: 4
Derived subgroup: [(0, 1, 2, 0), (1, 0, 0, 1), (1, 1, 1, 2), (1, 2, 2, 2)]
All three peripheral images have projective order3.
All three have the same class in A4/V4=C3.
The Fermat kernel ker(F2 -> (Z/3)^2) maps exactly onto V4.
Its peripheral loops are conjugates of A^3,B^3,C^3, all killed.
Thus each connected pullback component is a degree4 etale V4 cover of the compact cubic.
Over an algebraic closure this is the multiplication-by-two cover.
